<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36596" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plătēa</span></b> 
		(plătĕa, <i><span class="en">Cat. 15, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor.
			Ep. 2, 2, 71</span></i>), ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατεῖ?α</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A broad way in a city</i>, <i>a
			street</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quis hic est qui in plateam ingreditur?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 4, 1, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in hac habitasse plateă dictum est
					Chrysidem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 4, 5, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 1, 27</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">purae sunt plateae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 2, 71</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An open space in a house</i>, <i>an
				area</i>, <i>court-yard</i> (post-class.),
					<i><span class="en">Lampr. Elag. 24</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
